        "end_line": 770,
        "side": "new",
        "severity": "high",
        "category": "bug",
        "title": "Double free of mp_name when cpool was already initialized",
        "explanation": "mlx5_hws_cnt_pool_init copies pcfg into cpool->cfg, so cpool->cfg.name == mp_name. mlx5_hws_cnt_pool_destroy() frees cpool->cfg.name (line 798). On every error path where cpool != NULL (dcs_alloc failure, raw_data_alloc failure, action_create failure on host or guest port), the new mlx5_free(mp_name) frees the same buffer a second time, which can corrupt the heap.",
        "suggestion": "Free mp_name only when the pool has not taken ownership of it: `if (cpool == NULL) mlx5_free(mp_name);` placed before or instead of the unconditional free (or free it before calling destroy and clear cpool->cfg.name).",
        "evidence": "\tmlx5_free(mp_name);",
        "confidence": 0.8,
